on a new motion when folks are talking about how they actually really feel. I walk across the street and they're calling me a gook. People are like, I haven't been able to get a job for so long. I've stopped looking. And they say that they're getting beaten because people are saying, oh, that's the enemy. Go practice on him. So, you know, they're like, you know, how do we talk about this?
一个新的方向发展。有人说：“我走过马路，他们却叫我‘gook’（对亚洲人的蔑称）。”还有人说：“我好久都找不到工作了。我甚至已经放弃寻找了。”他们说自己挨打是因为别人会指着他们说：“看，那是敌人。去拿他练练手吧。”所以，你知道的，他们就在想：我们该怎么谈论这件事呢？

38
00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:36.000
Like, maybe we need to be able to figure out how we can all kind of come together and have a name and UG just throws it out. UG is like, you know, don't call us Oriano anymore. That's a rug. And Oriental is a rug. We are Asians and we are from America. Then they're like, ding, ding, ding. The lights go on.
就像是，也许我们需要弄清楚，我们该如何团结起来，起一个共同的名字。这时乌吉脱口而出。乌吉说：“听着，别再叫我们‘东方人’（Oriental）了。那是块地毯。”“东方人”是一块地毯。我们是亚裔，我们来自美国。然后他们就像是：叮、叮、叮，灵光一现。

