00:18:36.000 --> 00:19:01.000
You know, everybody's like excited. And they come out and they form a group that they call the Asian American political alliance. Asian American. It seems commonplace now. But this new political identity was radical. Up until then, U.S. immigration and military policy had forced Asian people to separate themselves. by nationality as a matter of survival. Just two decades earlier during World War II,
你知道的，所有人都兴奋起来了。他们聚在一起，成立了一个组织，并将其命名为“亚裔美国人政治同盟”（Asian American Political Alliance）。亚裔美国人。现在听起来这似乎很常见。但在当时，这种新的政治身份具有极大的颠覆性。在此之前，美国的移民和军事政策一直迫使亚裔为了生存，不得不按国籍将彼此隔离开来。就在仅仅二十年前的二战期间，

