Japanese Americans were being disappeared to internment camps. To distinguish themselves from the ethnically Japanese, Asian families would put signs in front of their homes and businesses that read, we are Chinese, we are Filipino, we are Korean. But now they were done with all that. That's 1968, and by 1969, there's thousands upon thousands of people all across the country
日裔美国人被强行带走并送往拘留营。为了将自己与日本血统区分开来，亚裔家庭会在他们的家门前和企业门口挂上牌子，上面写着：“我们是中国人，我们是菲律宾人，我们是韩国人。”但现在，他们受够了这一切。那是1968年，到了1969年，全美已有成千上万的人

